# Playwright Test Patterns

## Test Organization

Group tests by feature using `test.describe`. Use tags for selective execution.

```typescript
// tests/checkout/checkout.spec.ts
import { test, expect } from '../fixtures'

test.describe('Checkout flow', () => {
  test.beforeEach(async ({ page }) => {
    await page.goto('/cart')
  })

  test('completes purchase with valid card @smoke', async ({ page, checkoutPage }) => {
    await checkoutPage.fillCard('4242424242424242', '12/26', '123')
    await checkoutPage.submit()
    await expect(page).toHaveURL(/\/order-confirmation/)
  })

  test('shows error for declined card', async ({ page, checkoutPage }) => {
    await checkoutPage.fillCard('4000000000000002', '12/26', '123')
    await checkoutPage.submit()
    await expect(page.getByRole('alert')).toContainText('Your card was declined')
  })
})

// Run only @smoke tests in CI pre-deploy:
// npx playwright test --grep @smoke
```

## Network Interception and Mocking

Use `page.route()` to intercept requests and control API responses without hitting real backends.

```typescript
test('displays products from API', async ({ page }) => {
  // Intercept before navigation so no real request fires
  await page.route('**/api/products', async (route) => {
    await route.fulfill({
      status: 200,
      contentType: 'application/json',
      body: JSON.stringify([
        { id: '1', name: 'Widget', price: 9.99 },
        { id: '2', name: 'Gadget', price: 24.99 },
      ]),
    })
  })

  await page.goto('/products')
  await expect(page.getByTestId('product-card')).toHaveCount(2)
  await expect(page.getByText('Widget')).toBeVisible()
})

test('handles API error gracefully', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.route('**/api/products', (route) =>
    route.fulfill({ status: 500 })
  )

  await page.goto('/products')
  await expect(page.getByRole('alert')).toContainText('Failed to load products')
})

test('verifies request payload', async ({ page }) => {
  const requestPromise = page.waitForRequest('**/api/orders')

  await page.goto('/checkout')
  await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Place order' }).click()

  const request = await requestPromise
  const body = request.postDataJSON()
  expect(body).toMatchObject({ items: expect.any(Array), total: expect.any(Number) })
})
```

## API Testing with `request` Context

Use the built-in `request` fixture for direct API calls — no browser overhead.

```typescript
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test'

test('creates and retrieves a product via API', async ({ request }) => {
  const createResponse = await request.post('/api/products', {
    data: { name: 'New Widget', price: 14.99 },
  })
  expect(createResponse.ok()).toBeTruthy()
  const { id } = await createResponse.json()

  const getResponse = await request.get(`/api/products/${id}`)
  expect(getResponse.ok()).toBeTruthy()
  const product = await getResponse.json()
  expect(product).toMatchObject({ id, name: 'New Widget', price: 14.99 })
})
```

## Assertions

Prefer `expect` auto-retry assertions over manual waits. All `expect(locator)` assertions poll until they pass or time out.

```typescript
// ✅ Auto-retrying locator assertions — no manual waits needed
await expect(page.getByRole('status')).toHaveText('Saved')
await expect(page.getByTestId('spinner')).not.toBeVisible()
await expect(page).toHaveURL('/dashboard')
await expect(page).toHaveTitle(/Dashboard/)
await expect(page.getByRole('row')).toHaveCount(5)

// ✅ Soft assertions — collect all failures before failing the test
await expect.soft(page.getByTestId('price')).toContainText('$9.99')
await expect.soft(page.getByTestId('stock')).toContainText('In stock')
// Test continues even if the above fail; all soft errors reported together

// ❌ Avoid — fragile; doesn't retry on slow UI
const text = await page.getByTestId('status').textContent()
expect(text).toBe('Saved')
```

## Parallel Execution

Playwright runs spec files in parallel by default. Manage shared state carefully.

```typescript
// playwright.config.ts
export default defineConfig({
  workers: process.env.CI ? 2 : undefined, // Limit workers in CI to reduce flakiness
  fullyParallel: true,                      // Run tests within a file in parallel too

  // Retry flaky tests in CI only
  retries: process.env.CI ? 2 : 0,

  reporter: [
    ['html'],
    ['junit', { outputFile: 'results/junit.xml' }], // For CI integration
  ],
})
```

```typescript
// ✅ Test isolation — use unique data per test to avoid cross-test conflicts
test('user A can edit their profile', async ({ page }) => {
  const email = `user-${Date.now()}@example.com` // Unique per test run
  await createTestUser(email)
  // ...
})
```

## Visual Testing

Use `toHaveScreenshot()` for visual regression testing. Commit baseline screenshots.

```typescript
test('product page matches snapshot @visual', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.goto('/products/widget')
  await page.getByTestId('spinner').waitFor({ state: 'hidden' }) // Wait for async content

  // Mask dynamic elements (timestamps, ads) to prevent false failures
  await expect(page).toHaveScreenshot('product-page.png', {
    mask: [page.getByTestId('last-updated'), page.getByTestId('ad-banner')],
    maxDiffPixelRatio: 0.02, // Allow 2% pixel difference
  })
})
```

## Key Rules

- Each test must be independent — never depend on state from a previous test
- Use `test.describe.configure({ mode: 'serial' })` only when tests genuinely share state and can't be isolated
- `storageState` in `playwright.config.ts` sets the default auth for all tests — override per project for unauthenticated tests
- Run `npx playwright test --ui` locally for step-by-step debugging with time travel
- Artifacts (screenshots, videos, traces) auto-capture on failure in CI via `use: { trace: 'on-first-retry' }`
